  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "3c8e00a1-957c-4f94-b9e0-9202b1cacd91",
      "name": "📌 Overview – How This Workflow Works",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1392,
        1264
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 2,
        "width": 760,
        "height": 684,
        "content": "## 🔐 Vendor Security Risk Audit – AI Agent\n\n### How it works\nOn a weekly schedule, this workflow audits a vendor's security posture by running three parallel checks — fetching the vendor's website security headers, looking up domain age via RDAP, and checking for known data breaches via the HaveIBeenPwned API. All findings are compiled and passed to a GPT-4o-mini agent, which uses a structured output schema to produce a risk rating (Low / Medium / High / Critical), a list of security flags, and a plain-English recommendation. The result is written to a Google Sheets risk register. If the rating is High or Critical, a Slack alert goes to the security team and a summary email is sent. Two error paths ensure no failure goes unnoticed.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Connect **OpenAI API** to the OpenAI Chat Model node.\n2. Connect **Google Sheets OAuth2** and replace `YOUR_GOOGLE_SHEET_ID` in the Update Vendor Risk Register node. Create a `Vendor Risk Register` tab with the expected columns.\n3. Connect **Slack OAuth2** and replace `YOUR_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID` in both Alert and error nodes.\n4. Connect **Gmail OAuth2** and update `security-team@yourcompany.com` in the Send Summary Email node.\n5. Update the vendor name, website, contact email, and data access level in the `Set - Vendor Data` node.\n6. Adjust the schedule trigger frequency and activate."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "81a4e3b5-4d45-402d-a7af-3b2c5fb00ff1",
      "name": "Section – Vendor Setup & Parallel Security Checks",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -496,
        1600
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 872,
        "height": 792,
        "content": "## ⚙️ Vendor Setup & Parallel Security Checks\nThe schedule trigger fires and the vendor details are set (name, website, contact, data access level). Three checks then run in parallel: website security headers (HTTPS, HSTS, CSP, X-Frame), domain registration age via RDAP, and breach history from HaveIBeenPwned."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "f0b1ec69-36c3-4fc0-b366-a83a5d05f486",
      "name": "Section – AI Risk Analysis",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        400,
        1728
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 920,
        "height": 616,
        "content": "## 🤖 AI Risk Analysis\nAll three check results are merged and passed to the Vendor Risk Analysis Agent. GPT-4o-mini with a structured output schema returns: overall risk rating, security flags, a confidence score, and a recommended action. The output is parsed into a clean structured object."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "4480dea6-a2e9-4465-8533-8d21bad0d8cf",
